\n- Assignments: `quoteCount += 1`, `policy.remainingCap = ...` (2) = 12\n\n**Total Mass ≈ 72**\n\n### Step 3: Apply Simple Design Rules\n- **Rule 1 (Tests pass)**: green baseline confirmed.\n- **Rule 2 (Reveals intent)**: extract `handleQuoteStep` / `handleClaimStep` so `runScenario` reads as a clean dispatch loop. The `quoteCount` mutation is awkward; a `switch` over `step.op` also makes the exhaustive dispatch clearer.\n- **Rule 3 (No duplication)**: both branches call `results.push`; that repetition can be lifted so each handler returns a `Result` and the loop pushes once.\n- **Rule 4 (Fewest elements per unit)**: smaller focused functions.\n\n### Step 4: Implement"}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_15-50-57_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_opus-4-8-no-thinking/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/cli.ts\nPassing tests: 42\nRecent changes: added the claim-office CLI entry point (src/cli.ts) - reads a JSON scenario from stdin, processes quote/claim steps sequentially (tracking per-policy remaining cap and quote contract index), writes {results} JSON to stdout, exits non-zero with stderr message on error.\n\nRefactor src/cli.ts while keeping all tests green (run `pnpm test`) and keeping `npx tsc --noEmit` clean. Do not change src/claim-office.ts behavior. Run autonomously, return when done.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task: Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/cli.ts\nPassing tests: 42\nRecent changes: added the claim-office CLI entry point (src/cli.ts) - reads a JSON scenario from stdin, processes quote/claim steps sequentially (tracking per-policy remaining cap and quote contract index), writes {results} JSON to stdout, exits non-zero with stderr message on error.\n\nRefactor src/cli.ts while