 `BASE_PREMIUMS[item.type] ?? 0` appeared in both `mainItemsBasePremium` and `basePremiumForItem`. Consolidated to a single source of truth by reusing `basePremiumForItem` inside `mainItemsBasePremium` (moved it above so it's in scope). Now the \"how to compute an item's base premium\" knowledge lives in one place.\n\n**APP Mass (affected function: `mainItemsBasePremium`)**:\n\nBefore:\n```\n.filter((item) => !isComponent(item))\n.reduce((sum, item) => sum + (BASE_PREMIUMS[item.type] ?? 0), 0)\n```\n- Bindings: items, item, item, sum, item (5) = 5\n- Invocations: filter, isComponent, reduce, `+`, `??` index-access (`[]`) → count filter(2), isComponent(2), reduce(2), +(2), []/??(2) = 10\n- Loops: filter + reduce (2) = 10\n- Constants: 0 (2) = 2\n- **Total ≈ 27**\n\nAfter:\n```\n.filter((item) => !isComponent(item))\n.reduce((sum, item) => sum + basePremiumForItem(item), 0)\n```\n- Bindings: items, item, item, sum, item (5) = 5\n- Invocations: filter, isComponent, reduce, +, basePremiumForItem (5) = 10\n- Loops: filter + reduce (2) = 10\n- Constants: 0 (1) = 1\n- **Total ≈ 26**\n\nMass change: 27 → 26 (delta −1). More importantly, the duplicated lookup knowledge (Rule 3) is eliminated — the primary benefit here is maintainability, not raw mass.\n\n**Rule 4 (Fewest Elements)**: No unnecessary abstractions; each helper serves a distinct, tested purpose. No further simplification without hurting clarity (Rule 2).\n\nRefactoring Complete:\n- **Refactoring**: Removed duplicated base-premium lookup by reusing `basePremiumForItem` in `mainItemsBasePremium`\n- **Mass Change**: 27 → 26 for the affected function\n- **Tests**: All 17 passing"}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_15-50-57_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_opus-4-8-no-thinking/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 17\nRecent changes: added loyalty discount - customers with yearsWithMHPCO >= LOYALTY_YEARS_THRESHOLD (2) get a 20% (LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE) discount on the policy base premium; subtracted in quote's final sum.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green. Run tests with `pnpm test`. Run autonomously, return when done.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task: Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 17\nRecent changes: added loyalty discount - customers with yearsWithMHPCO >= LOYALTY_YEARS_THRESHOLD (2) get a 20% (LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE) discount on the policy base premium; subtracted in quote's final sum.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green. Run tests with `pnpm test`. Run autonomously, return when done."}],"timestamp":1784909048868},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Looking at the implementation and test files to understand how everything works together.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01YGfSLsAURK93JbDYGZMpFw","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.ts"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01MVnJUkY7uBLcEYKP2YAHf3","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.spec.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-opus-4-8@eu","usage":{"input":259,"output":121,"cacheRead":9704,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":10084,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784909048888,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-ef26b927-e1cd-4cd7-a470-6cea5ab743bf","responseModel":"claude-opus-4-8"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01YGfSLsAURK93JbDYGZMpFw","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"const PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\nconst FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.1;\nconst LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE = 0.2;\nconst LOYALTY_YEARS_THRESHOLD = 2;\nconst CURSE_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.5;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.3;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD = 5;\nconst COMPONENT_BASE_PREMIUM = 25;\nconst COMPONENT_BLOCK_SIZE = 3;\nconst COMPONENT_BLOCK_PREMIUM = 60;\nconst COMPONENT_TYPES = [\"rune\", \"moonstone\"];\nconst BASE_PREMIUMS: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 100,\n  amulet: 60,\n  staff: 80,\n  potion: 40,\n};\n\ntype Item = {\n  type: string;\n  material?: string;\n  enchantment?: number;\n  cursed?: boolean;\n};\n\nconst isComponent = (item: { type: string }): boolean =>\n  COMPONENT_TYPES.includes(item.type);\n\nconst componentGroupPremium = (count: number): number =>\n  count === COMPONENT_BLOCK_SIZE\n    ? COMPONENT_BLOCK_PREMIUM\n    : count * COMPONENT_BASE_PREMIUM;\n\nconst mainItemsBasePremium = (items: { type: string }[]): number =>\n  items\n    .filter((item) => !isComponent(item))\n    .reduce((sum, item) => sum + (BASE_PREMIUMS[item.type] ?? 0), 0);\n\nconst countByType = (items: { type: string }[]): Map<string, number> => {\n  const counts = new Map<string, number>();\n  for (const item of items) {\n    counts.set(item.type, (counts.get(item.type) ?? 0) + 1);\n  }\n  return counts;\n};\n\nconst componentsBasePremium = (items: { type: string }[]): number => {\n  const componentCounts = countByType(items.filter(isComponent));\n  return [...componentCounts.values()]\n    .map(componentGroupPremium)\n    .reduce((sum, premium) => sum + premium, 0);\n};\n\nconst basePremiumForItem = (item: Item): number =>\n  isComponent(item) ? COMPONENT_BASE_PREMIUM : (BASE_PREMIUMS[item.type] ?? 0);\n\nconst isHighEnchantment = (item: Item): boolean =>\n  (item.enchantment ?? 0) >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD;\n\nconst itemSurcharges = (item: Item): number => {\n  const base = basePremiumForItem(item);\n  const curseSurcharge = item.cursed ? base * CURSE_SURCHARGE_RATE : 0;\n  const highEnchantmentSurcharge = isHighEnchantment(item)\n    ? base * HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_SURCHARGE_RATE\n    : 0;\n  return curseSurcharge + highEnchantmentSurcharge;\n};\n\nexport const quote = (\n  customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: number },\n  items: Item[],\n  opts: unknown,\n): number => {\n  const basePremium =\n    mainItemsBasePremium(items) + componentsBasePremium(items);\n  const surcharges = items.reduce(\n    (sum, item) => sum + itemSurcharges(item),\n    0,\n  );\n  const firstInsuranceSurcharge = basePremium * FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE;\n  const loyaltyDiscount =\n    customer.yearsWithMHPCO >= LOYALTY_YEARS_THRESHOLD\n      ? basePremium * LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE\n      : 0;\n  return (\n    basePremium +\n    surcharges +\n    firstInsuranceSurcharge -\n    loyaltyDiscount +\n    PROCESSING_FEE\n  );\n};\n\nexport const claim = (): unknown => {\n  return undefined;\n};\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784909051263},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01MVnJUkY7uBLcEYKP2YAHf3","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { quote, claim } from \"./claim-office.js\";\n\ndescribe(\"Claim Office - quote: base premiums & fee\", () => {\n  it(\"empty item list -> premium 5 G (only processing fee)\", () => {\n    expect(quote({ yearsWithMHPCO: 0 }, [], { contractIndex: 0 })).toBe(5);\n  });\n  it(\"single sword (newcomer, first insurance) -> 100 base + 10 first + 5 fee = 115 G\", () => {\n    expect(\n      quote({ yearsWithMHPCO: 0 }, [{ type: \"sword\" }], { contractIndex: 0 }),\n    ).toBe(115);\n  });\n  it(\"single amulet -> 60 base + 6 first + 5 fee = 71 G\", () => {\n    expect(\n      quote({ yearsWithMHPCO: 0 }, [{ type: \"amulet\" }], { contractIndex: 0 }),\n    ).toBe(71);\n  });\n  it(\"single staff -> 80 base + 8 first + 5 fee = 93 G\", () => {\n    expect(\n      quote({ yearsWithMHPCO: 0 }, [{ type: \"staff\" }], { contractIndex: 0 }),\n    ).toBe(93);\n  });\n  it(\"single potion -> 40 base + 4 first + 5 fee = 49 G\", () => {\n    expect(\n      quote({ yearsWithMHPCO: 0 }, [{ type: \"potion\" }], { contractIndex: 0 }),\n    ).toBe(49);\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"Claim Office - quote: component building blocks (base premium)\", () => {\n  it(\"2 runes -> 50 G base premium (quote: 50 + 5 first + 5 fee = 60)\", () => {\n    expect(\n      quote({ yearsWithMHPCO: 0 }, [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }], {\n        contractIndex: 0,\n      }),\n    ).toBe(60);\n  });\n  it(\"3 runes -> 60 G base premium (block applies) (quote: 60 + 6 + 5 = 71)\", () => {\n    expect(\n      quote(\n        { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n        [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }],\n        { contractIndex: 0 },\n      ),\n    ).toBe(71);\n  });\n  it(\"4 runes -> 100 G base premium (no block - requires exactly 3) (quote 115)\", () => {\n    expect(\n      quote(\n        { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n        Array.from({ length: 4 }, () => ({ type: \"rune\" })),\n        { contractIndex: 0 },\n      ),\n    ).toBe(115);\n  });\n  it(\"7 runes -> 175 G base premium (quote 175 + 17.5 + 5 = 197.5)\", () => {\n    expect(\n      quote(\n        { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n        Array.from({ length: 7 }, () => ({ type: \"rune\" })),\n        { contractIndex: 0 },\n      ),\n    ).toBe(197.5);\n  });\n  it(\"2 runes + 1 moonstone -> 75 G base premium (no block: different types) (quote 87.5)\", () => {\n    expect(\n      quote(\n        { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n        [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"moonstone\" }],\n        { contractIndex: 0 },\n      ),\n    ).toBe(87.5);\n  });\n  it(\"3 runes + 3 moonstones -> 120 G base premium (two separate blocks) (quote 137)\", () => {\n    expect(\n      quote(\n        { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n        [\n          { type: \"rune\" },\n          { type: \"rune\" },\n          { type: \"rune\" },\n          { type: \"moonstone\" },\n          { type: \"moonstone\" },\n          { type: \"moonstone\" },\n        ],\n        { contractIndex: 0 },\n      ),\n    ).toBe(137);\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"Claim Office - quote: item-specific modifiers\", () => {\n  it(\"cursed sword (steel, ench 3), newcomer -> 165 G (100+50 curse+10 first+5 fee)\", () => {\n    expect(\n      quote(\n        { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n        [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3, cursed: true }],\n        { contractIndex: 0 },\n      ),\n    ).toBe(165);\n  });\n  it(\"sword enchantment 5 -> high-enchantment surcharge applies (100+30+10+5=145)\", () => {\n    expect(\n      quote(\n        { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n        [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 5, cursed: false }],\n        { contractIndex: 0 },\n      ),\n    ).toBe(145);\n  });\n  it(\"sword enchantment 4 -> no high-enchantment surcharge (115)\", () => {\n    expect(\n      quote(\n        { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n        [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 4, cursed: false }],\n        { contractIndex: 0 },\n      ),\n    ).toBe(115);\n  });\n  it(\"cursed sword enchantment 5 -> both curse and high-enchantment surcharges apply (100+50+30+10+5=195)\", () => {\n    expect(\n      quote(\n        { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n        [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 5, cursed: true }],\n        { contractIndex: 0 },\n      ),\n    ).toBe(195);\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"Claim Office - quote: policy-wide modifiers & scope\", () => {\n  it(\"cursed sword + plain amulet -> curse surcharge only on cursed item base (160 base + 50 curse + 16 first + 5 fee = 231)\", () => {\n    expect(\n      quote(\n        { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n        [\n          { type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3, cursed: true },\n          { type: \"amulet\", material: \"silver\", enchantment: 2, cursed: false },\n        ],\n        { contractIndex: 0 },\n      ),\n    ).toBe(231);\n  });\n  it(\"customer with exactly 2 years -> loyalty discount applies (100 - 20 loyalty + 10 first + 5 fee = 95)\", () => {\n    expect(\n      quote(\n        { yearsWithMHPCO: 2 },\n        [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3, cursed: false }],\n        { contractIndex: 0 },\n      ),\n    ).toBe(95);\n  });\n  it.todo(\"first insurance surcharge applies per quote regardless of history\");\n  it.todo(\"15% follow-up discount applies to each contract after the first quote in scenario\");\n});\n\ndescribe(\"Claim Office - quote: rounding in MHPCO's favor\", () => {\n  it.todo(\"premium yielding 197.5 G -> 198 G (rounded up)\");\n  it.todo(\"intermediate amounts kept as fractions; only final premium rounded\");\n});\n\ndescribe(\"Claim Office - quote: integration examples\", () => {\n  it.todo(\"newcomer with cursed sword (steel, ench 3) -> 165 G\");\n  it.todo(\"long-standing customer's second contract, cursed sword (steel, ench 7) -> 160 G\");\n});\n\ndescribe(\"Claim Office - quote: unknown item type\", () => {\n  it.todo(\"quote with unknown item type throws / errors\");\n});\n\ndescribe(\"Claim Office - claim: insurance sum & cap\", () => {\n  it.todo(\"policy of two swords -> insurance sum 2000 G, cap 4000 G\");\n  it.todo(\"policy of sword + amulet -> insurance sum 1600 G, cap 3200 G\");\n  it.todo(\"cursed sword -> cap 2000 G (based on unmodified insurance value)\");\n  it.todo(\"policy of sword + 3 runes block -> insurance sum 1750 G (block affects premium only)\");\n});\n\ndescribe(\"Claim Office - claim: standard reimbursement & deductible\", () => {\n  it.todo(\"regular sword (steel, ench 3), damage 500 -> payout 400 (500-100 deductible)\");\n  it.todo(\"rune (value 250), damage 200 -> payout 100 (200-100, no special clause)\");\n});\n\ndescribe(\"Claim Office - claim: special clauses\", () => {\n  it.todo(\"dragon sword, ench 8, damage 1000 -> payout 400 (50% clause then deductible)\");\n  it.todo(\"dragon sword, ench 9, damage 1000 -> payout 400 (both clauses; 50% wins, then deductible)\");\n  it.todo(\"dragon sword, ench 5, damage 800 -> payout 700 (dragon clause full, then deductible)\");\n  it.todo(\"steel sword, ench 9, damage 1000 -> payout 400 (high-ench 50% then deductible)\");\n});\n\ndescribe(\"Claim Office - claim: deductible per damage event\", () => {\n  it.todo(\"dragon attack damages sword (500) and amulet (300) -> payout 600 (deductible once per item)\");\n  it.todo(\"two swords damaged, two sword entries -> each treated as separate damage with own deductible\");\n  it.todo(\"more damage entries of a type than covered -> claim rejected (throws/errors)\");\n});\n\ndescribe(\"Claim Office - claim: cap exhaustion\", () => {\n  it.todo(\"sword cap 2000; first claim 1500 -> payout 1400, remaining 600\");\n  it.todo(\"sword cap 2000; second claim 1500 -> payout 600, remaining 0 (reduced to remaining cap)\");\n});\n\ndescribe(\"Claim Office - claim: rounding in MHPCO's favor\", () => {\n  it.todo(\"payout yielding 350.5 G -> 350 G (rounded down)\");\n});\n\ndescribe(\"Claim Office - claim: validation errors\", () => {\n  it.todo(\"damage references item not in policy -> claim rejected (throws/errors)\");\n  it.todo(\"damage entry with negative amount -> claim rejected (throws/errors)\");\n});\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784909051263},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I should run the tests to make sure everything's passing before moving forward.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01CnahHVhV5vaH9kmBDYef7T","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_15-50-57_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_opus-4-8-no-thinking && pnpm test 2>&1 | tail -20"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-opus-4-8@eu","usage":{"input":5054,"output":150,"cacheRead":9961,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":15165,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784909051263,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-ca6d9111-9e12-4374-96e3-69c4287aa6f7","responseModel":"c