gentScope":"both","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 24\nRecent changes: quote now validates item types up front, throwing an Error for unknown item types (isKnownItemType helper: component or present in BASE_PREMIUMS).\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green. Run tests with `pnpm test`. Run autonomously, return when done."}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-opus-4-8@eu","usage":{"input":686,"output":244,"cacheRead":79378,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":80308,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784909356756,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-178ca498-e024-4073-955f-288e704810e5","responseModel":"claude-opus-4-8"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_018Lgg6R9JooHtAK2GPyiT9P","toolName":"subagent","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 24 tests still green.\n\n## Refactoring Summary\n\n**Rule 1 (Tests Pass):** All 24 tests green before and after. ✓\n\n**Naming Evaluation (First Priority):** Existing names (`quote`, `isKnownItemType`, `isComponent`, `basePremiumForItem`, `itemSurcharges`, etc.) already clearly reveal intent — no renames needed. Added `assertKnownItemTypes`, whose `assert*` prefix signals a guard that throws.\n\n**Rule 2 (Reveals Intent) — applied:** Extracted the inline validation `for`/`if`/`throw` loop out of `quote` into a dedicated `assertKnownItemTypes` guard. This separates the \"validate inputs\" concern from the \"calculate premium\" concern, so `quote` now reads as a linear pipeline: validate → base premium → surcharges → modifiers → round.\n\n**Rule 3 (No Duplication):** No duplication introduced or found.\n\n**Rule 4 (Fewest Elements):** The extracted helper replaces an imperative loop with a single declarative `find`, keeping `quote`'s body leaner.\n\n### APP Mass — validation logic\n\n**Before (inlined loop in `quote`):**\n- loop `for...of`: 5\n- bindings (`item`, `items`): 2\n- conditional `if (!...)`: 4\n- invocations (`isKnownItemType`, `Error`): 4\n- constant (template string): 1\n\nTotal: **16**\n\n**After (`assertKnownItemTypes` helper):**\n- binding `unknownItem`: 1\n- invocation `items.find`: 2 + arrow invocation `isKnownItemType`: 2 = 4\n- conditional `if (unknownItem)`: 4\n- invocation `Error`: 2\n- constant (template string): 1\n\nTotal: **12** (in helper) + 1 invocation call site in `quote` (2) = **14**\n\n**Mass Change: 16 → 14 (delta −2)**, plus improved readability by removing the mutating loop in favor of a declarative `find`.\n\nRefactoring Complete:\n**Refactoring**: Extracted inline validation loop into `assertKnownItemTypes` guard (Rule 2 — reveals intent), converting an imperative loop to a declarative `find`.\n**Mass Change**: 16 → 14 (−2)\n**Tests**: All 24 passing"}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_15-50-57_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_opus-4-8-no-thinking/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 24\nRecent changes: quote now validates item types up front, throwing an Error for unknown item types (isKnownItemType helper: component or present in BASE_PREMIUMS).\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green. Run tests with `pnpm test`. Run autonomously, return when done.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task: Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 24\nRecent changes: quote now validates item types up front, throwing an Error for unknown item types (isKnownItemType helper: component or present in BASE_PREMIUMS).\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green. Run tests with `pnpm test`. Run autonomously, return when done."}],"timestamp":1784909360691},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I'll start by reading the implementation and test files."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01BA9yd6NqJZbmxNg5iZn81Q","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_15-50-57_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_opus-4-8-no-thinking/src/claim-office.ts"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01X9TfvdhnfbMb6eKwN2KAjH","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_15-50-57_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_opus-4-8-no-thinking/src/claim-office.spec.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-opus-4-8@eu","usage":{"input":216,"output":260,"cacheRead":9704,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":10180,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784909360711,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-da7f8aa1-da2f-4242-9f15-0ab9a1cc02b2","responseModel":"claude-opus-4-8"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01BA9yd6NqJZbmxNg5iZn81Q","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"const PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\nconst FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.1;\nconst LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE = 0.2;\nconst LOYALTY_YEARS_THRESHOLD = 2;\nconst FOLLOWUP_DISCOUNT_RATE = 0.15;\nconst CURSE_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.5;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.3;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD = 5;\nconst COMPONENT_BASE_PREMIUM = 25;\nconst COMPONENT_BLOCK_SIZE = 3;\nconst COMPONENT_BLOCK_PREMIUM = 60;\nconst COMPONENT_TYPES = [\"rune\", \"moonstone\"];\nconst BASE_PREMIUMS: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 100,\n  amulet: 60,\n  staff: 80,\n  potion: 40,\n};\n\ntype Item = {\n  type: string;\n  material?: string;\n  enchantment?: number;\n  cursed?: boolean;\n};\n\nconst isComponent = (item: { type: string }): boolean =>\n  COMPONENT_TYPES.includes(item.type);\n\nconst componentGroupPremium = (count: number): number =>\n  count === COMPONENT_BLOCK_SIZE\n    ? COMPONENT_BLOCK_PREMIUM\n    : count * COMPONENT_BASE_PREMIUM;\n\nconst basePremiumForItem = (item: Item): number =>\n  isComponent(item) ? COMPONENT_BASE_PREMIUM : (BASE_PREMIUMS[item.type] ?? 0);\n\nconst mainItemsBasePremium = (items: Item[]): number =>\n  items\n    .filter((item) => !isComponent(item))\n    .reduce((sum, item) => sum + basePremiumForItem(item), 0);\n\nconst countByType = (items: { type: string }[]): Map<string, number> => {\n  const counts = new Map<string, number>();\n  for (const item of items) {\n    counts.set(item.type, (counts.get(item.type) ?? 0) + 1);\n  }\n  return counts;\n};\n\nconst componentsBasePremium = (items: { type: string }[]): number => {\n  const componentCounts = countByType(items.filter(isComponent));\n  return [...componentCounts.values()]\n    .map(componentGroupPremium)\n    .reduce((sum, premium) => sum + premium, 0);\n};\n\nconst roundInInsurerFavor = (amount: number): number => Math.ceil(amount);\n\nconst isHighEnchantment = (item: Item): boolean =>\n  (item.enchantment ?? 0) >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD;\n\nconst itemSurcharges = (item: Item): number => {\n  const base = basePremiumForItem(item);\n  const curseSurcharge = item.cursed ? base * CURSE_SURCHARGE_RATE : 0;\n  const highEnchantmentSurcharge = isHighEnchantment(item)\n    ? base * HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_SURCHARGE_RATE\n    : 0;\n  return curseSurcharge + highEnchantmentSurcharge;\n};\n\nconst isKnownItemType = (item: { type: string }): boolean =>\n  isComponent(item) || item.type in BASE_PREMIUMS;\n\nexport const quote = (\n  customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: number },\n  items: Item[],\n  opts: { contractIndex: number },\n): number => {\n  for (const item of items) {\n    if (!isKnownItemType(item)) {\n      throw new Error(`Unknown item type: ${item.type}`);\n    }\n  }\n  const basePremium =\n    mainItemsBasePremium(items) + componentsBasePremium(items);\n  const surcharges = items.reduce(\n    (sum, item) => sum + itemSurcharges(item),\n    0,\n  );\n  const isLoyal = customer.yearsWithMHPCO >= LOYALTY_YEARS_THRESHOLD;\n  const isFollowupContract = opts.contractIndex >= 1;\n  const policyModifiers =\n    basePremium * FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE -\n    (isLoyal ? basePremium * LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE : 0) -\n    (isFollowupContract ? basePremium * FOLLOWUP_DISCOUNT_RATE : 0);\n  return roundInInsurerFavor(\n    basePremium + policyModifiers + surcharges + PROCESSING_FEE,\n  );\n};\n\nexport const claim = (): unknown => {\n  return undefined;\n};\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784909363981},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01X9TfvdhnfbMb6eKwN2KAjH","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { quote, claim } from \"./claim-office.js\";\n\ndescribe(\"Claim Office - quote: base premiums & fee\", () => {\n  it(\"empty item list -> premium 5 G (only processing fee)\", () => {\n    expect(quote({ yearsWithMHPCO: 0 }, [], { contractIndex: 0 })).toBe(5);\n  });\n  it(\"single sword (newcomer, first insurance) -> 100 base + 10 first + 5 fee = 115 G\", () => {\n    expect(\n      quote({ yearsWithMHPCO: 0 }, [{ type: \"sword\" }], { contractIndex: 0 }),\n    ).toBe(115);\n  });\n  it(\"single amulet -> 60 base + 6 first + 5 fee = 71 G\", () => {\n    expect(\n      quote({ yearsWithMHPCO: 0 }, [{ type: \"amulet\" }], { contractIndex: 0 }),\n    ).toBe(71);\n  });\n  it(\"single staff -> 80 base + 8 first + 5 fee = 93 G\", () => {\n    expect(\n      quote({ yearsWithMHPCO: 0 }, [{ type: \"staff\" }], { contractIndex: 0 }),\n    ).toBe(93);\n  });\n  it(\"single potion -> 40 base + 4 first + 5 fee = 49 G\", () => {\n    expect(\n      quote({ yearsWithMHPCO: 0 }, [{ type: \"potion\" }], { contractIndex: 0 }),\n    ).toBe(49);\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"Claim Office - quote: component building blocks (base premium)\", () => {\n  it(\"2 runes -> 50 G base premium (quote: 50 + 5 first + 5 fee = 60)\", () => {\n    expect(\n      quote({ yearsWithMHPCO: 0 }, [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }], {\n        contractIndex: 0,\n      }),\n    ).toBe(60);\n  });\n  it(\"3 runes -> 60 G base premium (block applies) (quote: 60 + 6 + 5 = 71)\", () => {\n    expect(\n      quote(\n        { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n        [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }],\n        { contractIndex: 0 },\n      ),\n    ).toBe(71);\n  });\n  it(\"4 runes -> 100 G base premium (no block - requires exactly 3) (quote 115)\", () => {\n    expect(\n      quote(\n        { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n        Array.from({ length: 4 }, () => ({ type: \"rune\" })),\n        { contractIndex: 0 },\n      ),\n    ).toBe(115);\n  });\n  it(\"7 runes -> 175 G base premium (quote 175 + 17.5 + 5 = 197.5 -> 198 rounded)\", () => {\n    expect(\n      quote(\n        { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n        Array.from({ length: 7 }, () => ({ type: \"rune\" })),\n        { contractIndex: 0 },\n      ),\n    ).toBe(198);\n  });\n  it(\"2 runes + 1 moonstone -> 75 G base premium (no block: different types) (quote 87.5 -> 88 rounded)\", () => {\n    expect(\n      quote(\n        { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n        [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"moonstone\" }],\n        { contractIndex: 0 },\n      ),\n    ).toBe(88);\n  });\n  it(\"3 runes + 3 moonstones -> 120 G base premium (two separate blocks) (quote 137)\", () => {\n    expect(\n      quote(\n        { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n        [\n          { type: \"rune\" },\n          { type: \"rune\" },\n          { type: \"rune\" },\n          { type: \"moonstone\" },\n          { type: \"moonstone\" },\n          { type: \"moonstone\" },\n        ],\n        { contractIndex: 0 },\n      ),\n    ).toBe(137);\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"Claim Office - quote: item-specific modifiers\", () => {\n  it(\"cursed sword (steel, ench 3), newcomer -> 165 G (100+50 curse+10 first+5 fee)\", () => {\n    expect(\n      quote(\n        { yearsWithMH