\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 29\nRecent changes: implemented claim(policyItems, incident) returning {payout, remainingCap}; payout sums (damage.amount - DEDUCTIBLE(100)) over incident.damages; remainingCap hardcoded 0 for now.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green. Run tests with `pnpm test`. Run autonomously, return when done."}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-opus-4-8@eu","usage":{"input":670,"output":270,"cacheRead":87900,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":88840,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784909525584,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-8b114c9e-5577-4c98-b63f-b8920aa7c083","responseModel":"claude-opus-4-8"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01A1ZdFmrfUBiiDRpVyL8EvQ","toolName":"subagent","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 29 tests still green.\n\n**Step 5: Refactored APP Mass**\n\n```ts\nconst reimbursementForDamage = (damage: Damage): number =>\n  damage.amount - DEDUCTIBLE;\n\nexport const claim = (policyItems, incident): ClaimResult => {\n  const payout = incident.damages.reduce(\n    (sum, damage) => sum + reimbursementForDamage(damage),\n    0,\n  );\n  return { payout, remainingCap: 0 };\n};\n```\n\n- `reimbursementForDamage`: bindings `damage` = 1; invocation `-` = 2 → subtotal 3\n- `claim`: constants `0`, `0` = 2; bindings `policyItems`, `incident`, `payout`, `sum`, `damage` = 5; invocations `reduce`, `+`, `reimbursementForDamage` = 3 → mass 6; loop `reduce` = 5\n\n**Total: 3 + 2 + 5 + 6 + 5 = 21**\n\n**Mass Change: 20 → 21 (delta +1)**\n\nMass rose by 1 because we replaced an inline `-` with a named invocation. **Rule 2 (Reveals Intent) trumps APP here**: the small mass increase buys a named domain concept (\"reimbursement for a damage = amount minus deductible\") consistent with the file's existing `basePremiumForItem` / `insuranceValueForItem` / `itemSurcharges` helper vocabulary. This also positions the code well for the upcoming special-clause tests, which will layer logic onto per-damage reimbursement.\n\n---\n\n## Refactoring Complete\n\n**Refactoring**: Extracted `reimbursementForDamage(damage)` helper from the inline `damage.amount - DEDUCTIBLE` in `claim`, revealing the per-damage reimbursement concept and matching the file's naming conventions.\n\n- **Naming**: `claim` kept (clear domain action); new helper named to reveal intent.\n- **Rule applied**: Rule 2 (Reveals Intent), accepted over Rule 4/APP.\n- **Mass Change**: 20 → 21 (delta +1, justified by clarity per \"Rule 2 trumps APP\").\n- **Tests**: All 29 passing."}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_15-50-57_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_opus-4-8-no-thinking/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 29\nRecent changes: implemented claim(policyItems, incident) returning {payout, remainingCap}; payout sums (damage.amount - DEDUCTIBLE(100)) over incident.damages; remainingCap hardcoded 0 for now.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green. Run tests with `pnpm test`. Run autonomously, return when done.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task: Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 29\nRecent changes: implemented claim(policyItems, incident) returning {payout, remainingCap}; payout sums (damage.amount - DEDUCTIBLE(100)) over incident.damages; remainingCap hardcoded 0 for now.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green. Run tests with `pnpm test`. Run autonomously, return when done."}],"timestamp":1784909529997},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm examining the implementation and test files to understand how everything works together.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01GNeN3tAU947eYEx45VL3BD","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.ts"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01KpgUGn6ri6DMHfrtcUzdNS","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.spec.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-opus-4-8@eu","usage":{"input":242,"output":122,"cacheRead":9704,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":10068,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784909530016,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-6f7e97e4-dee9-4eab-b9e0-7a20ed279c01","responseModel":"claude-opus-4-8"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01GNeN3tAU947eYEx45VL3BD","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"const PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\nconst FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.1;\nconst LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE = 0.2;\nconst LOYALTY_YEARS_THRESHOLD = 2;\nconst FOLLOWUP_DISCOUNT_RATE = 0.15;\nconst CURSE_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.5;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.3;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD = 5;\nconst COMPONENT_BASE_PREMIUM = 25;\nconst COMPONENT_BLOCK_SIZE = 3;\nconst COMPONENT_BLOCK_PREMIUM = 60;\nconst COMPONENT_TYPES = [\"rune\", \"moonstone\"];\nconst BASE_PREMIUMS: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 100,\n  amulet: 60,\n  staff: 80,\n  potion: 40,\n};\nconst INSURANCE_VALUES: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 1000,\n  amulet: 600,\n  staff: 800,\n  potion: 400,\n};\nconst COMPONENT_INSURANCE_VALUE = 250;\n\ntype Item = {\n  type: string;\n  material?: string;\n  enchantment?: number;\n  cursed?: boolean;\n};\n\nconst isComponent = (item: { type: string }): boolean =>\n  COMPONENT_TYPES.includes(item.type);\n\nconst componentGroupPremium = (count: number): number =>\n  count === COMPONENT_BLOCK_SIZE\n    ? COMPONENT_BLOCK_PREMIUM\n    : count * COMPONENT_BASE_PREMIUM;\n\nconst basePremiumForItem = (item: Item): number =>\n  isComponent(item) ? COMPONENT_BASE_PREMIUM : (BASE_PREMIUMS[item.type] ?? 0);\n\nconst mainItemsBasePremium = (items: Item[]): number =>\n  items\n    .filter((item) => !isComponent(item))\n    .reduce((sum, item) => sum + basePremiumForItem(item), 0);\n\nconst countByType = (items: { type: string }[]): Map<string, number> => {\n  const counts = new Map<string, number>();\n  for (const item of items) {\n    counts.set(item.type, (counts.get(item.type) ?? 0) + 1);\n  }\n  return counts;\n};\n\nconst componentsBasePremium = (items: { type: string }[]): number => {\n  const componentCounts = countByType(items.filter(isComponent));\n  return [...componentCounts.values()]\n    .map(componentGroupPremium)\n    .reduce((sum, premium) => sum + premium, 0);\n};\n\nconst roundInInsurerFavor = (amount: number): number => Math.ceil(amount);\n\nconst isHighEnchantment = (item: Item): boolean =>\n  (item.enchantment ?? 0) >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD;\n\nconst itemSurcharges = (item: Item): number => {\n  const base = basePremiumForItem(item);\n  const curseSurcharge = item.cursed ? base * CURSE_SURCHARGE_RATE : 0;\n  const highEnchantmentSurcharge = isHighEnchantment(item)\n    ? base * HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_SURCHARGE_RATE\n    : 0;\n  return curseSurcharge + highEnchantmentSurcharge;\n};\n\nconst isKnownItemType = (item: { type: string }): boolean =>\n  isComponent(item) || item.type in BASE_PREMIUMS;\n\nconst assertKnownItemTypes = (items: { type: string }[]): void => {\n  const unknownItem = items.find((item) => !isKnownItemType(item));\n  if (unknownItem) {\n    throw new Error(`Unknown item type: ${unknownItem.type}`);\n  }\n};\n\nexport const quote = (\n  customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: number },\n  items: Item[],\n  opts: { contractIndex: number },\n): number => {\n  assertKnownItemTypes(items);\n  const basePremium =\n    mainItemsBasePremium(items) + componentsBasePremium(items);\n  const surcharges = items.reduce(\n    (sum, item) => sum + itemSurcharges(item),\n    0,\n  );\n  const isLoyal = customer.yearsWithMHPCO >= LOYALTY_YEARS_THRESHOLD;\n  const isFollowupContract = opts.contractIndex >= 1;\n  const policyModifiers =\n    basePremium * FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE -\n    (isLoyal ? basePremium * LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE : 0) -\n    (isFollowupContract ? basePremium * FOLLOWUP_DISCOUNT_RATE : 0);\n  return roundInInsurerFavor(\n    basePremium + policyModifiers + surcharges + PROCESSING_FEE,\n  );\n};\n\nconst insuranceValueForItem = (item: { type: string }): number =>\n  isComponent(item)\n    ? COMPONENT_INSURANCE_VALUE\n    : (INSURANCE_VALUES[item.type] ?? 0);\n\nexport const insuranceSum = (items: { type: string }[]): number =>\n  items.reduce((sum, item) => sum + insuranceValueForItem(item), 0);\n\nconst DEDUCTIBLE = 100;\n\ntype Damage = { itemType: string; amount: number };\ntype Incident = { cause: string; damages: Damage[] };\ntype ClaimResult = { payout: number; remainingCap: number };\n\nexport const claim = (\n  policyItems: Item[],\n  incident: Incident,\n): ClaimResult => {\n  const payout = incident.damages.reduce(\n    (sum, damage) => sum + (damage.amount - DEDUCTIBLE),\n    0,\n  );\n  return { payout, remainingCap: 0 };\n};\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784909533154},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01KpgUGn6ri6DMHfrtcUzdNS","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { quote, claim, insuranceSum } from \"./claim-office.js\";\n\ndescribe(\"Claim Office - quote: base premiums & fee\", () => {\n  it(\"empty item list -> premium 5 G (only processing fee)\", () => {\n    expect(quote({ yearsWithMHPCO: 0 }, [], { contractIndex: 0 })).toBe(5);\n  });\n  it(\"single sword (newcomer, first insurance) -> 100 base + 10 first + 5 fee = 115 G\", () => {\n    expect(\n      quote({ yearsWithMHPCO: 0 }, [{ type: \"sword\" }], { contractIndex: 0 }),\n    ).toBe(115);\n  });\n  it(\"single amulet -> 60 base + 6 first + 5 fee = 7