roject","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 42\nRecent changes: added assertDamageAmountsValid guard - claim throws for damage entries with negative amounts.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green. Run tests with `pnpm test`. Run autonomously, return when done.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task: Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 42\nRecent changes: added assertDamageAmountsValid guard - claim throws for damage entries with negative amounts.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green. Run tests with `pnpm test`. Run autonomously, return when done."}],"timestamp":1784910004251},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm examining the implementation and test files to understand how everything works together.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_017bQqC57sCw9SgKkZ9TC7xt","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_15-50-57_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_opus-4-8-no-thinking/src/claim-office.ts"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01BSNz1Q1Jrjo2qX3NHFasJE","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_15-50-57_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_opus-4-8-no-thinking && pnpm test 2>&1 | tail -20"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-opus-4-8@eu","usage":{"input":198,"output":267,"cacheRead":9704,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":10169,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784910004272,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-4840db2c-4db9-4e3a-aeee-9e77b1d3590c","responseModel":"claude-opus-4-8"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_017bQqC57sCw9SgKkZ9TC7xt","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"const PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\nconst FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.1;\nconst LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE = 0.2;\nconst LOYALTY_YEARS_THRESHOLD = 2;\nconst FOLLOWUP_DISCOUNT_RATE = 0.15;\nconst CURSE_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.5;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.3;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD = 5;\nconst COMPONENT_BASE_PREMIUM = 25;\nconst COMPONENT_BLOCK_SIZE = 3;\nconst COMPONENT_BLOCK_PREMIUM = 60;\nconst COMPONENT_TYPES = [\"rune\", \"moonstone\"];\nconst BASE_PREMIUMS: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 100,\n  amulet: 60,\n  staff: 80,\n  potion: 40,\n};\nconst INSURANCE_VALUES: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 1000,\n  amulet: 600,\n  staff: 800,\n  potion: 400,\n};\nconst COMPONENT_INSURANCE_VALUE = 250;\n\ntype Item = {\n  type: string;\n  material?: string;\n  enchantment?: number;\n  cursed?: boolean;\n};\n\nconst isComponent = (item: { type: string }): boolean =>\n  COMPONENT_TYPES.includes(item.type);\n\nconst componentGroupPremium = (count: number): number =>\n  count === COMPONENT_BLOCK_SIZE\n    ? COMPONENT_BLOCK_PREMIUM\n    : count * COMPONENT_BASE_PREMIUM;\n\nconst basePremiumForItem = (item: Item): number =>\n  isComponent(item) ? COMPONENT_BASE_PREMIUM : (BASE_PREMIUMS[item.type] ?? 0);\n\nconst mainItemsBasePremium = (items: Item[]): number =>\n  items\n    .filter((item) => !isComponent(item))\n    .reduce((sum, item) => sum + basePremiumForItem(item), 0);\n\nconst countByType = (items: { type: string }[]): Map<string, number> => {\n  const counts = new Map<string, number>();\n  for (const item of items) {\n    counts.set(item.type, (counts.get(item.type) ?? 0) + 1);\n  }\n  return counts;\n};\n\nconst componentsBasePremium = (items: { type: string }[]): number => {\n  const componentCounts = countByType(items.filter(isComponent));\n  return [...componentCounts.values()]\n    .map(componentGroupPremium)\n    .reduce((sum, premium) => sum + premium, 0);\n};\n\n// Both premiums and payouts round \"in MHPCO's favor\", but in opposite\n// directions: premiums round up (customer pays more), payouts round down\n// (MHPCO pays less).\nconst roundPremiumInInsurerFavor = (amount: number): number =>\n  Math.ceil(amount);\nconst roundPayoutInInsurerFavor = (amount: number): number =>\n  Math.floor(amount);\n\nconst isHighEnchantment = (item: Item): boolean =>\n  (item.enchantment ?? 0) >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD;\n\nconst itemSurcharges = (item: Item): number => {\n  const base = basePremiumForItem(item);\n  const curseSurcharge = item.cursed ? base * CURSE_SURCHARGE_RATE : 0;\n  const highEnchantmentSurcharge = isHighEnchantment(item)\n    ? base * HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_SURCHARGE_RATE\n    : 0;\n  return curseSurcharge + highEnchantmentSurcharge;\n};\n\nconst isKnownItemType = (item: { type: string }): boolean =>\n  isComponent(item) || item.type in BASE_PREMIUMS;\n\nconst assertKnownItemTypes = (items: { type: string }[]): void => {\n  const unknownItem = items.find((item) => !isKnownItemType(item));\n  if (unknownItem) {\n    throw new Error(`Unknown item type: ${unknownItem.type}`);\n  }\n};\n\nexport const quote = (\n  customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: number },\n  items: Item[],\n  opts: { contractIndex: number },\n): number => {\n  assertKnownItemTypes(items);\n  const basePremium =\n    mainItemsBasePremium(items) + componentsBasePremium(items);\n  const surcharges = items.reduce(\n    (sum, item) => sum + itemSurcharges(item),\n    0,\n  );\n  const isLoyal = customer.yearsWithMHPCO >= LOYALTY_YEARS_THRESHOLD;\n  const isFollowupContract = opts.contractIndex >= 1;\n  const policyModifiers =\n    basePremium * FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE -\n    (isLoyal ? basePremium * LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE : 0) -\n    (isFollowupContract ? basePremium * FOLLOWUP_DISCOUNT_RATE : 0);\n  return roundPremiumInInsurerFavor(\n    basePremium + policyModifiers + surcharges + PROCESSING_FEE,\n  );\n};\n\nconst insuranceValueForItem = (item: { type: string }): number =>\n  isComponent(item)\n    ? COMPONENT_INSURANCE_VALUE\n    : (INSURANCE_VALUES[item.type] ?? 0);\n\nexport const insuranceSum = (items: { type: string }[]): number =>\n  items.reduce((sum, item) => sum + insuranceValueForItem(item), 0);\n\nconst DEDUCTIBLE = 100;\nconst CAP_MULTIPLIER = 2;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_CLAIM_THRESHOLD = 8;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_REIMBURSEMENT_RATE = 0.5;\n\ntype Damage = { itemType: string; amount: number };\ntype Incident = { cause: string; damages: Damage[] };\ntype ClaimResult = { payout: number; remainingCap: number };\n\nconst capForPolicy = (policyItems: Item[]): number =>\n  CAP_MULTIPLIER * insuranceSum(policyItems);\n\nconst qualifiesForHighEnchantmentClause = (item: Item): boolean =>\n  (item.enchantment ?? 0) >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_CLAIM_THRESHOLD;\n\nconst reimbursementForDamage = (damage: Damage, item: Item): number => {\n  const reimbursed = qualifiesForHighEnchantmentClause(item)\n    ? damage.amount * HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_REIMBURSEMENT_RATE\n    : damage.amount;\n  return reimbursed - DEDUCTIBLE;\n};\n\nconst assertDamageAmountsValid = (damages: Damage[]): void => {\n  for (const damage of damages) {\n    if (damage.amount < 0) {\n      throw new Error(`Invalid damage amount: ${damage.amount}`);\n    }\n  }\n};\n\nconst assertDamagesWithinCoverage = (\n  policyItems: Item[],\n  damages: Damage[],\n): void => {\n  const coveredCounts = countByType(policyItems);\n  const damagedCounts = countByType(\n    damages.map((damage) => ({ type: damage.itemType })),\n  );\n  for (const [type, count] of damagedCounts) {\n    if (count > (coveredCounts.get(type) ?? 0)) {\n      throw new Error(`Damage for uncovered item: ${type}`);\n    }\n  }\n};\n\nconst totalReimbursement = (\n  policyItems: Item[],\n  damages: Damage[],\n): number =>\n  damages.reduce((sum, damage) => {\n    const item = policyItems.find((i) => i.type === damage.itemType)!;\n    return sum + reimbursementForDamage(damage, item);\n  }, 0);\n\nexport const claim = (\n  policyItems: Item[],\n  incident: Incident,\n  remainingCap: number = capForPolicy(policyItems),\n): ClaimResult => {\n  assertDamageAmountsValid(incident.damages);\n  assertDamagesWithinCoverage(policyItems, incident.damages);\n  const rawPayout = totalReimbursement(policyItems, incident.damages);\n  const payout = roundPayoutInInsurerFavor(Math.min(rawPayout, remainingCap));\n  return { payout, remainingCap: remainingCap - payout };\n};\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784910008007},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01BSNz1Q1Jrjo2qX3NHFasJE","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n> tdd-experiment-run@ test /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_15-50-57_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_opus-4-8-no-thinking\n> vitest run\n\n\n RUN  v1.6.1 /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_15-50-57_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_opus-4-8-no-thinking\n\n ✓ src/claim-office.spec.ts  (42 tests) 5ms\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  42 passed (42)\n   Start at  16:20:07\n   Duration  180ms (transform 38ms, setup 0ms, collect 38ms, tests 5ms, environment 0ms, prepare 51ms)\n\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784910008007},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm looking at the assertion functions used in the `claim` method and noticing a pattern. The `assertDamageAmountsValid` function uses a for loop that could be refactored to use `.find` instead, similar to how `assertKnownItemTypes` is structured.\n\nRefactoring to use `.find`... This refactoring reduces the cognitive mass while maintaining consistency with the existing pattern, so I'll go ahead and apply it.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"I'll analyze the implementation and apply a refactoring. Let me examine the recently added code alongside the existing patterns.\n\n**Naming Evaluation (First Priority)**:\n- `assertDamageAmountsValid` — clearly reveals intent (throws when damage amounts are invalid). ✓ Keep.\n- All other names (`totalReimbursement`, `reimbursementForDamage`, `capForPolicy`, etc.) accurately describe their purpose. ✓ Keep.\n\n**Rule 3 — Conceptual Duplication (chosen refactoring)**:\nThe new `assertDamageAmountsValid` uses an imperative `for`/`if`/`throw` loop, while the sibling guard `assertKnownItemTypes` expresses the identical concept (\"find the first offending entry, then throw\") with the declarative `.find()` pattern. This is conceptual duplication with inconsistent expression. Aligning them improves clarity (Rule 2) and consistency (Rule 3).\n\n**Current Code Mass** (`assertDamageAmountsValid`):\n- Bindings: `damages`, `damage` = 2\n- Constants: `0` literal, template string = 2\n- Invocations: `new Error` = 2\n- Conditionals: `if` = 4\n- Loops: `for...of` = 5\n- **Total: 15**"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_019iebNLYrwR6Ld1TUe9rNGD","name":"edit","arguments":{"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_15-50-57_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_opus-4-8-no-thinking/src/claim-office.ts","edits":[{"oldText":"const assertDamageAmountsValid = (damages: Damage[]): void => {\n  for (const damage of damages) {\n    if (damage.amount < 0) {\n      throw new Error(`Invalid damage amount: ${damage.amount}`);\n    }\n  }\n};","newText":"const assertDamageAmountsValid = (damages: Damage[]): void => {\n  const invalidDamage = damages.find((damage) => damage.amount < 0);\n  if (invalidDamage) {\n    throw new Error(`Invalid damage amount: ${invalidDamage.amount}`);\n  }\n};"}]}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-opus-4-8@eu","usage":{"input":3784,"output":1764,"cacheRead":9704,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":15252,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784910008007,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-8ed8db19-7446-4540-9f0c-0f51a851eed4","responseModel":"claude-opus-4-8"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"t