ls intent — kept.\n\n**Mass Change**: 15 → 13 (delta −2, loop eliminated)\n**Tests**: All 42 passing"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-opus-4-8@eu","usage":{"input":692,"output":543,"cacheRead":13930,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":15165,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1784910029195,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-e4c3bba2-1d03-48dc-8316-0b7eb7ef3739","responseModel":"claude-opus-4-8"}],"stderr":"","usage":{"input":9363,"output":2706,"cacheRead":43042,"cacheWrite":0,"cost":0,"contextTokens":15165,"turns":4},"model":"requesty/vertex/claude-opus-4-8@eu","stopReason":"stop"}]},"isError":false,"timestamp":1784910035312},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 42 tests pass. Now I need to create the CLI entry point at `src/cli.ts` per the spec. This orchestrates the scenario: reads JSON from stdin, processes steps sequentially, writes results. Let me verify my `quote`/`claim` signatures fit the CLI needs, then build the CLI.\n\nThe CLI must track: quote step's items (for later claims referencing that policy) and the running remaining cap per policy. Let me write the CLI."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01J1etzo982cTmTEhtxVccNx","name":"write","arguments":{"content":"#!/usr/bin/env node\nimport { quote, claim, insuranceSum } from \"./claim-office.js\";\n\ntype Item = {\n  type: string;\n  material?: string;\n  enchantment?: number;\n  cursed?: boolean;\n};\n\ntype Damage = { itemType: string; amount: number };\ntype Incident = { cause: string; damages: Damage[] };\n\ntype QuoteStep = { op: \"quote\"; items: Item[] };\ntype ClaimStep = { op: \"claim\"; policy: number; incident: Incident };\ntype Step = QuoteStep | ClaimStep;\n\ntype Scenario = {\n  customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: number };\n  steps: Step[];\n};\n\ntype Result = { premium: number } | { payout: number; remainingCap: number };\n\nconst CAP_MULTIPLIER = 2;\n\nconst readStdin = (): Promise<string> =>\n  new Promise((resolve, reject) => {\n    let data = \"\";\n    process.stdin.setEncoding(\"utf8\");\n    process.stdin.on(\"data\", (chunk) => (data += chunk));\n    process.stdin.on(\"end\", () => resolve(data));\n    process.stdin.on(\"error\", reject);\n  });\n\ntype PolicyState = { items: Item[]; remainingCap: number };\n\nconst runScenario = (scenario: Scenario): Result[] => {\n  const { customer, steps } = scenario;\n  const policies = new Map<number, PolicyState>();\n  let quoteCount = 0;\n  const results: Result[] = [];\n\n  steps.forEach((step, index) => {\n    if (step.op === \"quote\") {\n      const premium = quote(customer, step.items, {\n        contractIndex: quoteCount,\n      });\n      quoteCount += 1;\n      policies.set(index, {\n        items: step.items,\n        remainingCap: CAP_MULTIPLIER * insuranceSum(step.items),\n      });\n      results.push({ premium });\n    } else if (step.op === \"claim\") {\n      const policy = policies.get(step.policy);\n      if (!policy) {\n        throw new Error(`Claim references unknown policy: ${step.policy}`);\n      }\n      const result = claim(policy.items, step.incident, policy.remainingCap);\n      policy.remainingCap = result.remainingCap;\n      results.push({\n        payout: result.payout,\n        remainingCap: result.remainingCap,\n      });\n    } else {\n      throw new Error(`Unknown operation: ${(step as { op: string }).op}`);\n    }\n  });\n\n  return results;\n};\n\nconst main = async (): Promise<void> => {\n  try {\n    const input = await readStdin();\n    const scenario = JSON.parse(input) as Scenario;\n    const results = runScenario(scenario);\n    process.stdout.write(JSON.stringify({ results }));\n  } catch (error) {\n    process.stderr.write(\n      `Error: ${error instanceof Error ? error.message : String(error)}\\n`,\n    );\n    process.exit(1);\n  }\n};\n\nmain();\n","path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_15-50-57_claim-office-example-ma